WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.998 --> 00:00:02.561
- [Narrator] The sound you hear emanating

00:00:02.561 --> 00:00:05.822
from your speakers,
that low, ominous tone,

00:00:05.822 --> 00:00:09.393
is not a signal problem or
a defect of poor recording.

00:00:09.393 --> 00:00:11.743
It's but a sample of what
brings us all the way

00:00:11.743 --> 00:00:13.406
to the American Southwest,

00:00:13.406 --> 00:00:15.756
to investigate an infamous phenomenon

00:00:15.756 --> 00:00:17.839
known simply as The Taos hum.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:23.134
This October, on Friday the 13th,

00:00:23.134 --> 00:00:25.893
from an executive producer
of The Walking Dead,

00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:28.413
and an executive producer of The X-files,

00:00:28.413 --> 00:00:29.995
comes six terrifying tales,

00:00:29.995 --> 00:00:32.693
based on the podcast phenomenon, Lore.

00:00:32.693 --> 00:00:35.365
Until then, we offer you this short film,

00:00:35.365 --> 00:00:37.789
inspired by the series.

00:00:37.789 --> 00:00:39.149
- I'm Steve Iannuccilli.

00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:41.048
I'm a professor of anatomy and physiology

00:00:41.048 --> 00:00:42.324
at St. Joseph's College.

00:00:42.324 --> 00:00:44.277
The Taos Hum is a strange
phenomenon that happens

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:46.627
in a town called Taos, New Mexico.

00:00:46.627 --> 00:00:49.362
What it is basically is people in Taos,

00:00:49.362 --> 00:00:51.257
about two percent of the people, hear this

00:00:51.257 --> 00:00:54.313
strange humming sound
or this buzzing sound

00:00:54.313 --> 00:00:56.804
that really irritates them,
gets into their heads,

00:00:56.804 --> 00:00:59.338
gives them headaches, gives
them anxiety, gives them fears,

00:00:59.338 --> 00:01:02.682
and people don't know really
where it's coming from.

00:01:02.682 --> 00:01:04.140
- [Narrator] This persistent sound

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:06.105
emerges seemingly from nowhere

00:01:06.105 --> 00:01:09.399
and plagues those who hear it
day and night without relief.

00:01:09.399 --> 00:01:11.615
First thought to be a disorder consistent

00:01:11.615 --> 00:01:13.874
with the high-pitched ringing of tinnitus,

00:01:13.874 --> 00:01:16.028
doctors have become puzzled
by patients' accounts

00:01:16.028 --> 00:01:17.927
that they are able to move freely toward

00:01:17.927 --> 00:01:20.143
or away from the phantom sound.

00:01:20.143 --> 00:01:23.230
- They describe it as maybe a
low rumble of a diesel engine

00:01:23.230 --> 00:01:25.607
or maybe a really loud refrigerator noise.

00:01:25.607 --> 00:01:27.782
- [Narrator] And while the
description of the sound

00:01:27.782 --> 00:01:30.247
is consistent from all
who claim to hear it,

00:01:30.247 --> 00:01:32.421
the intensity varies widely.

00:01:32.421 --> 00:01:34.404
A dull annoyance to some

00:01:34.404 --> 00:01:37.410
but an unyielding nightmare for others.

00:01:37.410 --> 00:01:39.164
- It ruins people's lives because they can

00:01:39.164 --> 00:01:40.832
never get away from the sound.

00:01:40.832 --> 00:01:44.198
All day, all the time, in
your ears, in your head.

00:01:44.198 --> 00:01:45.637
Some people have been driven to suicide

00:01:45.637 --> 00:01:47.324
because of the Taos Hum.

00:01:47.324 --> 00:01:49.864
It really does affect the
patients really badly.

00:01:49.864 --> 00:01:52.105
- [Narrator] Some scientists theorize

00:01:52.105 --> 00:01:55.442
that the hum could be caused
by regional seismic shifts,

00:01:55.442 --> 00:01:58.530
while others blame low
frequency radio signals

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:01.830
used by the military at
classified sites in the desert.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.470
- If you wanna go down
the conspiracy route,

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:05.676
some people talk about the U.S. Military

00:02:05.676 --> 00:02:07.196
using ELF technology.

00:02:07.196 --> 00:02:09.122
ELF technology could also
be used against your enemies

00:02:09.122 --> 00:02:12.111
as a type of warfare where it will cause

00:02:12.111 --> 00:02:14.874
headaches, and it will cause
noises to be heard in the ears

00:02:14.874 --> 00:02:16.346
and ringing in the ears, and it will drive

00:02:16.346 --> 00:02:18.339
your enemies crazy if
you make the frequency

00:02:18.339 --> 00:02:20.832
perfect to where it really irritates them.

00:02:20.832 --> 00:02:22.983
- [Narrator] Others
still look to the Navajo,

00:02:22.983 --> 00:02:26.219
Apache, and Hopi teachings
that identify the hum

00:02:26.219 --> 00:02:28.266
as the song of long lost spirits

00:02:28.266 --> 00:02:31.930
trying to speak to us from the other side.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:33.813
- [Steve] New Mexico is one of those areas

00:02:33.813 --> 00:02:36.423
that's still rich in the
culture of the Native Americans,

00:02:36.423 --> 00:02:39.113
and they believe that it's the Earth.

00:02:39.113 --> 00:02:41.446
The Earth is talking to you.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:45.362
- [Narrator] In the end, we
may never truly understand

00:02:45.362 --> 00:02:47.664
the origin or meaning behind the sound,

00:02:47.664 --> 00:02:50.402
and it seems those affected
must resign themselves

00:02:50.402 --> 00:02:53.228
to its effect or uproot their entire lives

00:02:53.228 --> 00:02:55.846
to move away from it, but somewhere,

00:02:55.846 --> 00:02:58.318
resonating in the depths
beneath the surface,

00:02:58.318 --> 00:03:01.573
the unseen source
continues to faithfully hum

00:03:01.573 --> 00:03:03.823
for anyone who will listen.

00:03:10.074 --> 00:03:12.657
(tone ringing)

